% Abstract
%

\begin{abstract}

We report the results of a joint 3-flavour oscillation analysis
performed by the {\em VaLOR} (Valencia-Lancaster-Oxford-Rutherford) 
group using the latest 2012 
T2K oscillation analysis framework on the Run 1+2+3 dataset.
This dataset corresponds to an integrated JPARC 
neutrino beam exposure of 3.020 $\times10^{20}$ POT.

This analysis performed a joint determination of 
$|\Delta m^{2}|$, $sin^{2}\theta_{23}$, $sin^{2}\theta_{13}$ and $\delta_{CP}$ 
with a simultaneous oscillation fit to both the single 
$\mu$-like ring and single e-like ring event samples.
The oscillation fit was performed in a 3-flavour framework
including matter effects in constant density matter.

The motivation for performing a joint oscillation analysis 
and a detailed description of the fitting method are presented.
The results obtained by the joint analysis are compared 
with the ones obtained by the stand-alone $\nu_{e}$-appearance and
$\nu_{\mu}$-disappearance analyses.

\end{abstract}

